    "content": "VIDEO EDITING BEST PRACTICES - PROMETHEUS KNOWLEDGE BASE 1. FUNDAMENTAL EDITING PRINCIPLES 1.1 The Invisible Edit The best edit is the one the audience never notices. Every cut should serve the narrative or maintain visual continuity. Prometheus prioritizes edits that: \u2022 Preserve eye-line continuity across shots \u2022 Maintain consistent screen direction (180-degree rule) \u2022 Cut on action (motion motivates the transition) \u2022 A void jump cuts on static subjects unless stylistically intentional 1.2 Pacing & Rhythm Pacing is determined by shot duration, not just cut frequency: \u2022 Dialogue scenes : Hold on speaker for 2-3 seconds after line delivery to let emotional beats land. Cut to listener reaction before cutting back. \u2022 Action sequences : Cut on impacts, use shorter durations (0.5-2 seconds), vary shot scale to maintain energy. \u2022 Montage sequences : Accelerate pacing progressively; start with 2-second shots, end with 0.5second shots to build momentum. \u2022 Emotional beats : Linger on close-ups; 4-6 seconds minimum for moments of vulnerability, revelation, or decision. 1.3 The J-Cut and L-Cut \u2022 J-Cut: Audio from the next shot begins before the video cuts. Creates anticipation and smooths transitions. Use for scene introductions. \u2022 L-Cut: Audio from the current shot continues over the next shot's video. Maintains continuity and bridges spatial transitions. Use for dialogue overlap and scene exits. \u2022 Prometheus default: Apply J-cuts to",
