    "content": "\u2022 Smash cut : Abrupt cut from quiet to loud or vice versa. Use for comedic or horror impact. Ensure 6+ dB level difference. Generated by Kimi.ai 5. COMMON TECHNICAL MISTAKES TO A VOID 1. Flash F rames: Single black or incorrectly exposed frames between cuts. Always check 1 frame before and after each cut point. 2. Audio Pops : Cuts at zero-crossings cause clicks. Apply 2-4 frame crossfades on all audio cuts unless hard sync is required. 3. Mismatched Eyelines : If character A looks screen-left in shot 1, character B must look screenright in shot 2. Reverse if crossing the line. 4. Jump Cuts : A void cutting between two shots of the same subject with similar framing. Use cutaway, B-roll, or dissolve. 5. Over-normalization: Bringing all audio to the same level destroys dynamic range. Preserve 6-12 dB range in dialogue. 6. Over-sharpening: Excessive sharpening creates halos and noise. Apply sharpening only in final delivery pass, never in proxies. 7. W rong Color Space Export : Exporting Rec. 709 content as sRGB or vice versa causes gamma shift. Always tag output color space correctly. 6. WORKFLOW OPTIMIZATION 6.1 Proxy W orkflow \u2022 Proxy ratio : 1/4 resolution (1080p->540p, 4K->1080p) at ProRes Proxy or H.264 low bitrate for smooth editing. \u2022 Relink strategy : Maintain original folder structure. Prometheus auto-generates proxies with preserved metadata for seamless relink. \u2022 Smart rendering : Only re-render changed segments.",
